cctext patch 0004: kerning.

plutovg advanced every glyph by its advance width alone: text came out a
little wider than a browser's, labels ("AV", "To", "y.") visibly loose, and
Mermaid's box sizes (measured through the same code) drifted from
Chromium's. Text now goes through one layout function
(plutovg_font_face_layout) that adds the pair adjustment stb_truetype
reads from the font -- GPOS pair positioning (formats 1 and 2), else the
kern table -- between consecutive glyphs; drawing
(plutovg_canvas_add_text / fill_text / stroke_text) and measuring
(plutovg_font_face_text_extents) share it, so what lunasvg measures is
what it draws. New API: plutovg_font_face_get_text_path and
plutovg_font_face_traverse_text_path (a run's outline as drawn).

resvg's test suite: text 59 -> 188 of 379 (the suite renders with kerning
on, as browsers do).

Apply after 0003.

